  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of Cr₄Ni₈S₁₆ (Cr(NiS₂)₂) crystallizes in the monoclinic space group C2/c (No. 15), with 28 atoms in the unit cell distributed over four independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis identifies Cr centers coordinated by six S neighbors, while Ni centers are tetrahedrally coordinated by four S neighbors, with Ni–S distances of 2.049–2.207 Å. The S centers show three geometric neighbors, typically two Cr and one Ni or one Cr and two Ni. Validated polyhedron-sharing analysis reveals corner-sharing between Ni tetrahedra, and both corner- and edge-sharing between Cr six-vertex and Ni tetrahedral polyhedra, forming a three-dimensional periodic connectivity network.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
